{
 "id": "mof-pore-screen",
 "tab": "materials",
 "material": "mof",
 "title": "Which known MOFs have pore windows sized for lithium sieving?",
 "question": "How many known MOFs have pore-limiting diameters in a range useful for separating lithium from magnesium in brine?",
 "headline": {
  "value": "10,804",
  "unit": "MOFs",
  "text": "10,804 of 12,863 distinct known MOFs (84%) have pore windows wider than a water molecule (2.65 A) but narrower than a hydrated Mg2+ ion (8.56 A), the geometric range for ion sieving; only 423 sit in the narrow band between hydrated Li+ and Mg2+. Candidate chemistry is plentiful; making oriented, defect-free membranes is the open problem. Geometry only, not selectivity."
 },
